Vikram and Betal: The Wise Merchant

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a merchant who was very wise,” said Betal. “He always thought carefully before making decisions.”

One day, two men came to him with a problem.

They both claimed ownership of the same bag of money.

The merchant listened quietly.

Then he said, “Leave the bag with me. Come back tomorrow.”

That night, the merchant opened the bag and found a small note inside.

It had the name of the real owner written on it.

The next day, both men returned.

The merchant asked each of them, “What is inside the bag?”

One man answered correctly and calmly.

The other man gave a wrong answer.

The merchant gave the bag to the honest man.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, how did the merchant make the right decision?”

Vikram replied, “He used both patience and intelligence to find the truth.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Think carefully before making decisions.
